  8.7 PSON_L INPUT

   The PSON_L is an internally pulled-up (3.3 V) input signal to enable/disable the main output V1 of the front-end. This active-low
   pin is also used to clear any latched fault condition. The timing diagram is given in Figure 13 and the parameters in Table 5.

  OPERATING CONDITION                                                                                                    MIN                MAX             UNIT
  tPSON_L V1on          PSON_L to V1 delay (on)                                                                               2              20             ms
  tPSON_L V1off         PSON_L to V1 delay (off)                                                                              2              20             ms
  tPSON_L H min         PSON_L minimum High time                                                                          10                                ms

                                                              Table 5. PSON_L timing




